From: yinjiayi <yinjiayi@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Pass the original basic-string object and byte range

SPDX-License-Identifier: LGPL-2.1-or-later
Upstream: https://github.com/activesys/libcstl/tree/f0fd5ccb817192614588915ab0b5dbebbc6ed58b
Upstream-Status: Not submitted; downstream original-test type compatibility.

Exact-head CI 38741530253 rejects two original unit-test arguments with
GCC 14 -Wincompatible-pointer-types. The invalid-pby-string test allocates
a basic_string_t and changes its _pby_string member: pass that object, not
the address of the local pointer. The cstr range test initializes the same
ten string_t elements through the helper's declared _byte_t* interface.
Keep all allocations, sentinel values, ten elements, assertions, cleanup,
registered tests, library algorithms and strict compiler options unchanged.
Remove when upstream corrects these two original test arguments.

--- a/test/ut/ut_cstl_basic_string_aux.c
+++ b/test/ut/ut_cstl_basic_string_aux.c
@@ -32,7 +32,7 @@
 {
     basic_string_t* pbstr = create_basic_string(int);
     pbstr->_pby_string = (_byte_t*)0xff;
-    assert_false(_basic_string_is_created(&pbstr));
+    assert_false(_basic_string_is_created(pbstr));
     pbstr->_pby_string = NULL;
     basic_string_destroy(pbstr);
 }
@@ -650,7 +650,7 @@
     {
         assert_true(strcmp((char*)basic_string_at(pbstr, i), "abcdefg") == 0);
     }
-    _basic_string_init_elem_range_auxiliary(pbstr, elems, 10);
+    _basic_string_init_elem_range_auxiliary(pbstr, (_byte_t*)elems, 10);
     for(i = 0; i < 10; ++i)
     {
         assert_true(strcmp(string_c_str(elems+i), "") == 0);
